  "rules": [
    "When history shows a sustained downtrend followed by a single positive spike (e.g., Example 1), the model fails to capture immediate volatility and consistently underestimates the first 3-5 days of the forecast horizon.",
    "The model exhibits severe mean-reversion bias in volatile regimes; it predicts a smooth upward drift while true outcomes show sharp peaks followed by rapid, deep corrections (e.g., Examples 1-4).",
    "In low-sentiment or neutral environments with high historical volatility, the model's forecast horizon is too long and linear, ignoring the 'spike-and-crash' pattern typical of EU ETS price discovery.",
    "When sentiment history contains mixed signals (positive/negative) amidst a volatile trend, the model ignores the momentum reversal risk inherent in the first 10 days of the forecast window.",
    "The model systematically underestimates short-term upside potential during recovery phases but fails to account for subsequent downside volatility within the same 30-day window."
  ]
